YAPAP [Tournament] bourland-Hea-Gno-Fem-Neu (25120 points)

A few days after 20,000,000 point Priest offed himself with a scroll
of genocide typo, I decided to give the lowest score a shot and
whipped up a Gnomish Healer.  The first 2 or so failed due to pet
pitfalls, but a 3rd went on to nearly empty the dungeon, but without
any blood on her hands.

The story started the same as usual, with careful pet manangement
simulating a game of tag where I didn't want to be it.  For kicks i
immediately made my scalpel dull at -3, but was careful to avoid the
newts and lichen.  Dlvl2 brought great luck, with a small general
store with a permantent lightsource and a soon converted altar, which
allowed for quick item identification.  Since food levels were good, I
headed towards the Mines first, and after some close calls ducked into
the colaigned altar and came out a protected man.  Another permanent
lightsource and a magic whistle was found in a hardware store, so I
headed towards sokoban to see which DSM type I should get.  The Oracle
brought me to lvl3, and Sokoban's amulet resulted in me wishing for
GDSM.

At this point, I was sitting pretty, although afraid of the ever
present danger of a newt or lichen around the corner.  The next bit of
luck occured directly below Sokoban, where the bones of poisonous
corpse eater who aparently visited a huge scroll shop also left a few
rings and a magic marker.  Back to my stash my feline army and I went
and most of my stuff was IDed, including a /oPoly.  The choice was
made to do some early polypiling, which oddly resulted in 8 ?oGen and
a =oSD.  Not going for style points, this conduct was quickly broken,
which saw the disappearance of twLch, follwed by the too easy to kill
Z:x.  With a decent pet warhorse in need of food, I left F off the
list for now, and wielding a creampie I felt pretty safe.

Dlvl13 saw a poly trap and a saddle, which turned all my pets except
my now ridable warhorse into non-eating &s.  Went to minetown to buy
the remaining protection, and all the shopkeeps except the candle
maker found their end.  Feeling a little safer with a decent AC, down
to the castle I went, digging past and procrastinating Medusa by
teleporting her out of her room, and sneaking in the back way I was
the owner of the castle wand (0:2).  A few zaps later I had scrolls of
charging, a blessed Archon figurine, the Eye of Aethiopica, and a new
plan of action.

Back to Sokoban I went and camp was set, my Archon created, and
?oEarth->Rocks->Meatballs->Rations.  Using my marker to write and off
fort ruining Giants, I soon found myself surrounded my boulders and
casting create monster over and over again.  Unicorn horns and paper
golems became scrolls of genocide, and with time, I genocided the
worthless, and was soon alone with my Archon.  The loot was gathered,
alchemy done, and soon my Archon was lvl49 and myself lvl30.  We were
no longer alone, and thousands of turns later, we were again admist
heaps of treasure.  The smoky healing potion pile brought a backup
Archon figurine and some assorted spellbooks that would come in handy,
and I was now ready to continue.

Into the dungeon we decended to meet HD17 or higher creatures and aoon
all that would appear were Titans, Ki-Rin and the room filling
creatures they would summon.  Soon each level was filled up and
creatures were jumping down the holes they created, and a mess was at
hand.  After charming most of hte Titan and Ki-Rin and using conflict
the 5-8 levels they messed up were cleared and our party was now
Harold, the Playful Archon and his nutty new lady friend, Maude, the
rideable Ki-Rin.  Down down we went and Archons were the next course. 
Camp was set and with time, even they wouldn't appear and I was sad to
discover Harold was alone having offed the ferile Maude.

Down down we went, getting the 2 of the 3 needed items and skipping
the Medusa problem with the Eye.  The valley found new creatures, but
forts were made and soon it was empty.  Hell went in record time, and
my leashed Archon stayed by my side all the way to the vibrating
square, where I let him play for a bit before we invoked back to our
stash.

Then came a moment of brilliance, as I (for the first time in years)
poofed my BoH by replacing my wand in the wrong bag.  Gone were all my
cursed gain level potions, magic markers, wands of wishing and
polymorph, my backup Archon, and pretty much everything of use.  Most
of my rings were on person, as was my lightsource.  Resorting through
all the junk, i found my spare BoH in my icebox, and filled it with
some holy water and paper and the one magic marker (0:83) and /oTel
(0:7) I had set aside.  Soon we were off, at the Wizard's frontdoor,
where I realized that I had no candles anymore as well.  So, back to
minetown we went, and fortunately the only remaining creature there
still had 7 for sale. ;)

Finally on track, Harold retrieved the Book (after filling in the
water in case the Wizard died over it), and the amulet followed.  In
the sanctum was my luckiest find - one blessed potion of gain level,
which soon became cursed and was saved for later.  The climb was
typical, but empty, and /oTel and my TC made it as quick as possible. 
Medusa was skipped, spells releaned at my loot, and the Dlvl1 stairs
were entered.

Earth saw the Wizard fall for the 2nd and final time, and the empty
planes were comically easy.  Jumping boots and teleporting the priests
aways made for a quick Astral.  First I tried Death, but Famine was
the neutral one.  Locking the door to keep Harld and my Angel out, I
stripped myself of everything but the amulet, and the offering was
made...

